+// spellings no longer exist on this host, so injecting them leaves this entry
+// pending and the whole plugin tree fails to activate.
+//
+// `jobs` is required: without a job registry there is nothing to report, and
+// every base-backed profile provides it. `webServer` is a web-seat service that
+// only a composition mounting the web carrier provides, so the route is
+// registered from `ctx.inject(['webServer'], ...)` — the documented way to keep
+// an optional registration (the harness's own /api bridge does the same in
+// @deepseek-ai/dsh-api-gateway). A hard `webServer` inject would leave this row
